**Example 5.** Find a least square polynomial degree 5 for \(f(x)\!=\!\frac{1}{1\!+\!x}\), in the interval \(2\!\leq\!x\!\leq\!\) using the weight function

\[w(x)\!=\!\frac{1}{\sqrt{(x\!-\!2)(5\!-\!x)}}\]

which stresses the importance of the errors at \(t\) ends of the interval.

Reduction to interval \([-1,1]\), \(t\!=\!\frac{2x\!-\!7}{3}\)

\[w(x(t))\!=\!\frac{2}{3}\,\frac{1}{\sqrt{1\!-\!t^{2}}}\]

From \(22.2\), \(f_{m}(t)\!=\!T_{m}(t)\) and

\[a_{m}\!=\!\frac{4}{3\pi}\int_{-1}^{1}\frac{1}{\sqrt{1\!-\!t^{2}}}\,\frac{1}{t\! +\!3}\;T_{m}(t)dt\qquad(m\!\neq\!0)\]